        "content": "<p>I have succeeded in getting the parsing rules, but I couldn't find (even with the help of AI) the registrations of elaborator rules? I assume those are dynamically stored somewhere in the compiler state. Do I need anything more than syntax and elaboration rules do be complete with regards to a hermetically sealed evaluation outside of the lean runtime?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getProductionRulesForCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Environment</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">categoryName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cats</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">parserExtension</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getState</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">categories</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c23</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cats</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">find!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">categoryName</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c23</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">kinds</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Use runCoreM to provide the MonadEnv context that `#eval` needs</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">liftCoreM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getEnv</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getProductionRulesForCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`command</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Found {rules.length} command syntax rules.\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s!</span><span class=\"s2\">\" - {rule}\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
