    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, that's what I want to do, a toy runtime in Rust for learning and hacking. For that I need to understand how the parser and the elaborator work.</p>\n<p>I extracted the parsing rules, and now I also am able to extract the elaboration rules.</p>\n<p>One thing that's confusing me, aren't there supposed to be way more elaboration rules in mathlib?</p>\n<p>Found 188 elaboration rules. Most of them are in Lean.Elab, only a few are in mathlib.</p>\n<p>If I remove the mathlib import there are only 114 elaboration rules. Does 74 elaboration rules in mathlib only sound reasonable?</p>",
